{
  "system": "spacemit-k3",
  "description": "SpacemiT K3: 8 X100 cores (cpus 0-7, VLEN 256) and 8 A100 AI cores (cpus 8-15, VLEN 1024). Facts measured on our board; see k3-work/experiments/k3-measurements.md.",
  "default_dispatch_target": "any",
  "notes": {
    "kinds": "kind 'x100' = cpus 0-7, kind 'a100' = cpus 8-15. Ingest maps XPU-RT's CPU_P to x100 and CPU_E to a100 (--cpu-p-kind x100 --cpu-e-kind a100).",
    "ime": "smt.vmadot runs on ALL 8 X100 cores (K1 kernels bit-exact on cpus 0-7, 2026-10-19; unlike the K1, where only 0-3 have it) with the 4x8x4 tile, and on the A100 cores with the 8x16x8 tile. The same encoding means different tiles: K1 (ime_x60) kernels on an A100 return wrong answers (max_abs_err=48); ime2_a100 kernels trap on an X100 (vlenb check).",
    "impls": "Per-core 'impls' lists the kernel families that are legal on that kind: x100 rvv + ime (ime_x60), a100 rvv + ime2 (ime2_a100). Read by the ingest legality check.",
    "ai_label": "Pinning a thread to cpus 8-15 fails (EINVAL) until it writes its tid to /proc/set_ai_thread; after that its allowed set is 8-15 and new threads inherit the permission. Never label a thread that must run on an X100.",
    "tensor_pairs": "cpus 8 and 9 each ran at 0.89 of solo speed when both used the matrix unit (one shared tensor unit per pair, as the K3 paper says); other pairs are untested.",
    "clock": "rdtime runs at 24 MHz on both kinds; X100 2.2 GHz, A100 1.8 GHz."
  },
